3
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:53,433
About Time

4
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:58,639
I always knew my family was a little strange, starting with me

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:02,037
Too lanky, too skinny, and her hair is such an orange color

6
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:05,028
My mom was lovely, but she had a lot of things different from other moms

7
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:06,513
Mom was very independent

8
00:01:06,600 --> 00:01:09,672
Unique, always busy, and cool-headed

9
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:11,552
Mom's fashion icon was Queen

10
00:01:12,480 --> 00:01:16,917
Dad was more ordinary. He always had plenty of time.

11
00:01:17,040 --> 00:01:20,316
When he retired from teaching at the university for his 50th birthday

12
00:01:20,440 --> 00:01:23,716
Now he talks to me and even loses to me at ping pong

13
00:01:23,840 --> 00:01:25,637
So he can live out the rest of his life comfortably.

14
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:29,238
And there was Desmond, my mom's brother.

15
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:33,393
Uncle always dressed impeccably, all put together like that.

16
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:35,078
He didn't do much.

17
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:38,073
Uncle was a very charming and intelligent man.

18
00:01:38,840 --> 00:01:41,991
He was always thinking about something else, but we never figured out what it was.

19
00:01:42,240 --> 00:01:45,038
And lastly, Catherine.

20
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,839
My little sister, Katie, as some call her.

21
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:51,510
With her discerning jacket and haircut among the family,

22
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:54,194
there was an angel.

23
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:59,115
Fairy-like eyes and feet always in purple socks.

24
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,708
It was like that then, and it's still like that now.

25
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:04,553
She is the most wonderful thing in this world.

26
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:09,478
Overall, it was a happy childhood without anything particularly unusual.

27
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:13,639
We drank tea at the beach every day until I turned twenty-one.

28
00:02:13,760 --> 00:02:16,558
While playing water games and eating sandwiches.

29
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:20,030
Regardless of whether it was summer or winter weather.

30
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:26,879
We watched movies every Friday night.

31
00:02:27,760 --> 00:02:29,751
No matter the weather.

32
00:02:30,720 --> 00:02:34,952
And once a year, there was a terrible New Year's Eve party.

33
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,751
Want another one?

34
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:59,673
You're really great.

35
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:03,275
I'm Katie. What am I drinking?

36
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,917
This is very expensive.

37
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,394
Cheers - Cheers.

38
00:03:22,320 --> 00:03:23,753
It's almost midnight already.

39
00:03:23,840 --> 00:03:25,831
Let's go. Let's go.

40
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:27,837
So I can find you a girl...

41
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,793
Oh my god!

42
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:34,755
Everyone makes mistakes. It's okay.

43
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:37,998
...6, 5.

44
00:03:38,120 --> 00:03:41,112
4, 3, 2, 1.

45
00:03:41,280 --> 00:03:45,512
Happy New Year!

46
00:03:47,440 --> 00:03:48,429
Sorry.

47
00:04:00,440 --> 00:04:05,116
The next morning, I woke up feeling hungover and ashamed of myself.

48
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:09,193
Unaware that it would be the day my life would change forever.

49
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:11,872
Get up, dummy.

50
00:04:14,520 --> 00:04:15,999
Dad's calling.

51
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:18,714
Hi, sexy pajamas.

52
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,877
Tim, come in.

53
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:27,319
Over here.

54
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:29,639
Sit down.

55
00:04:31,680 --> 00:04:33,671
You're being very formal.

56
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,156
Right.

57
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:38,032
When I turned twenty-one, I had the same experience as my father,

58
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:43,593
and because my life changed so much after that,

59
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:48,635
I approach it cautiously.

60
00:04:48,720 --> 00:04:49,709
Okay.

61
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:53,119
Tell me when you're ready. Something feels very suspicious.

62
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,189
Right.

63
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:59,476
Tim, son...

64
00:05:01,160 --> 00:05:06,234
Simply put, the men in our family have always...

65
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:09,196
It might sound strange,

66
00:05:09,720 --> 00:05:13,315
don't be too surprised. Be mentally prepared.

67
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:16,358
This is a family secret.

68
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:21,037
That secret is that the men in our family

69
00:05:23,760 --> 00:05:25,637
