Okay.

152
00:11:30,480 --> 00:11:31,959
Thanks.

153
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:35,389
Well then...

154
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,279
You're good at this.

155
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,279
It's my specialty.

156
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,152
It was a summer of tanning and suffering.

157
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,037
I called my dumb friend Jay over to play tennis.

158
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:57,395
I thought I would stand out around Jay.

159
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,269
But I didn't!

160
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:06,672
—What are you doing?—Oh dear.

161
00:12:10,280 --> 00:12:12,236
Charlotte made us both look like idiots.

162
00:12:12,320 --> 00:12:13,799
Bad luck, Team.

163
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:21,000
How can you focus on the game under these circumstances?

164
00:12:21,640 --> 00:12:25,997
How am I supposed to live life in a situation like this?

165
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:30,319
Time passed like that, without anything getting better.

166
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:32,910
And then the day she leaves came.

167
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:35,789
Charlotte, this is our last lunch together.

168
00:12:35,920 --> 00:12:37,148
No!

169
00:12:37,480 --> 00:12:40,790
I really enjoyed spending the summer with you.

170
00:12:40,920 --> 00:12:43,115
—Right.—Thank you.

171
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,919
—It was great.—Isn't it, Desmond?

172
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:49,476
—What?—She said it was nice spending the summer with Charlotte.

173
00:12:49,840 --> 00:12:51,319
Charlotte? Who's Charlotte?

174
00:12:51,440 --> 00:12:53,670
Snap out of it, I mean Charlotte, she's sitting next to you.

175
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:58,310
—Ah, right, Charlotte.—Me.

176
00:12:59,120 --> 00:13:00,519
Nice to meet you.

177
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,310
Didn't you have a great time spending the summer with Charlotte, Team?

178
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:10,949
Yes.

179
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:13,359
August flew by so fast.

180
00:13:13,560 --> 00:13:15,471
You taught me so much, didn't you?

181
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,028
Yes, in a much more sophisticated way.

182
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,873
I want to think of it as a quiet way.

183
00:13:34,720 --> 00:13:36,073
Come in.

184
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:39,628
—Charlotte.—Yeah.

185
00:13:43,560 --> 00:13:47,189
Since tonight is the last night, can I ask you something?

186
00:13:48,080 --> 00:13:49,832
Go ahead, ask.

187
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,479
Wait a minute.

188
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:55,912
It’s not about love, is it?

189
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,593
Love? Why?

190
00:13:57,720 --> 00:14:01,235
Kitcat warned me if I said something like that.

191
00:14:01,400 --> 00:14:05,837
He told me not to treat you like a little sister and act stupid.

192
00:14:05,920 --> 00:14:07,399
He told me to be clear.

193
00:14:08,280 --> 00:14:11,272
Or did I just make myself look like an idiot for nothing?

194
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,676
Did you come here to ask my secret to playing tennis well one last time?

195
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:17,351
No, it is about love.

196
00:14:17,440 --> 00:14:19,112
Really?

197
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:22,555
That's sweet.

198
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:26,676
I regret waiting until the last night.

199
00:14:26,800 --> 00:14:31,635
You should have come to my room when there was time.

200
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,795
So, was 'last night' a bad idea?

201
00:14:34,960 --> 00:14:39,795
Very bad, actually. It feels kind of insulting how to think about it.

202
00:14:40,240 --> 00:14:42,470
There's nothing you can do on a 'last night.'

203
00:14:43,120 --> 00:14:46,112
You know, I get it.

204
00:15:06,560 --> 00:15:07,913
Come in.

205
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:11,231
- Hi Tim - Charlotte

206
00:15:12,640 --> 00:15:14,312
- Hi - Sit down.

207
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,678
I don't know if you noticed, but

208
00:15:19,840 --> 00:15:23,435
for the last month, I've been completely obsessed with you.

209
00:15:25,160 --> 00:15:27,833
It's only natural.

210
00:15:28,080 --> 00:15:32,073
Because you have the face of a goddess,

211
00:15:32,200 --> 00:15:33,952
and hair too.

212
00:15:34,280 --> 00:15:37,272
But even if you weren't pretty,

213
00:15:38,280 --> 00:15:40,953
even if you had no hair at all...

214
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:43,760
For any medical reason,

215
00:15:45,200 --> 00:15:47,156
I would still have admired you.

216
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:48,669
So, listen...

217
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:53,876
I wanted to know if you felt the same way about me.

218
00:15:55,200 --> 00:15:56,189
Wow.

219
00:15:57,520 --> 00:15:59,397
Let's do this.

220
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:05,956
Can we live together over the summer and then ask again on our last night?

221
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:09,637
- Last night? - Sure.

222
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,993
We'll talk on the last night; we'll see how things turn out then.

223
00:16:14,960 --> 00:16:16,234
Isn't that interesting?

224
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:17,629
Right.

225
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:22,438
No, that's a perfect plan. Absolutely perfect, the last night.

226
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:23,993
The last night.

227
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:28,438
Thanks.

228
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:31,113
Goodnight, Timmy.

229
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:40,391
I learned a huge lesson.

230
00:16:40,560 --> 00:16:43,711
That no matter how much time travel you do, you can't make someone love you.

231
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:44,829
Bye!

232
00:16:46,040 --> 00:16:48,235
And so, the love of my life left.

233
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:53,514
And the next day was my turn to leave.

234
00:16:56,280 --> 00:16:59,272
Here, don't use it all at once.

235
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:01,949
Thank you.

236
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:07,393
Don't call too often. Your mom doesn't like being bothered.

237
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,670
Okay, thanks.

238
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:32,471
I boarded a train to London looking for the future and a woman.

239
00:17:35,120 --> 00:17:37,395
I ended up living in St. John's Wood near Abbey Road

240
00:17:37,480 --> 00:17:40,631
with Harry, my father's playwright friend.

241
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:44,674
When going somewhere unfamiliar, having connections helps.

242
00:17:57,600 --> 00:18:01,354
What kind of jerk is he?

243
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,989
- I'm James's son - Who?

244
00:18:07,200 --> 00:18:09,316
- James Lake - What's that?

245
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,752
I heard you were renting out a room.

246
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:17,594
Go in and wait.

247
00:18:18,600 --> 00:18:21,910
Quietly, don't make a sound.

248
00:18:22,840 --> 00:18:24,432
Or I'll kill you.

249
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:37,554
When you rang the doorbell, for the first time in ten years,

250
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,198
a good idea popped into my head.

251
00:18:39,880 --> 00:18:41,632
But now I forgot it.

252
00:18:42,400 --> 00:18:44,356
Damn it.

253
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,072
How's your dad?

254
00:18:46,360 --> 00:18:50,478
I always thought he was weird. There was something suspicious about your dad.

255
00:18:50,600 --> 00:18:53,956
- Really? - Yeah, I didn't really like him either.

256
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:57,514
Is your mom still as beautiful as Andy Warhol?

257
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:58,629
Excuse me?

258
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:02,594
This is my wife.

259
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:05,752
- She's pretty. - Yeah, she wasn't a great impression at first.

260
00:19:07,080 --> 00:19:08,991
She mocks people a lot.

261
00:19:10,120 --> 00:19:12,270
But as you live,

262
00:19:12,760 --> 00:19:15,433
you realize she's the most wonderful woman in the world.

263
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:18,430
So she must have left me.

264
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,558
Here.

265
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:26,954
Don't be too loud, especially when we're having sex.

266
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:28,635
There won't be any chances for that.

267
00:19:28,720 --> 00:19:31,439
Damn, two idiots living under one roof.

268
00:19:31,960 --> 00:19:33,791
This is my daughter.

269
00:19:35,120 --> 00:19:38,795
If you want, there seems to be no one who hasn't slept with her,

270
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,548
so it wasn't an environment where you could dream of romance.

271
00:19:44,320 --> 00:19:46,959
It was the same at work.

272
00:19:47,400 --> 00:19:50,119
The world of law seems full of men.

273
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:56,632
Hi, I'm Lori. Nice to meet you. It's nice to meet you too.

274
00:19:57,120 --> 00:20:00,749
Who knows, maybe we'll become best friends.

275
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:03,838
- Who are you? - I'm Tim Lake.

276
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:06,071
He's better than this clown.

277
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:09,877


278
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:11,558


279
00:20:11,640 --> 00:20:14,200


280
00:20:16,280 --> 00:20:20,876


281
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:23,514


282
00:20:23,640 --> 00:20:26,871


283
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:31,519
No matter how many women there were in the world,

284
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:34,757
I only had Lori with me.

