Delicious? Really?

1117
01:15:56,520 --> 01:15:58,636
I feel good since you said it was delicious.

1118
01:16:06,480 --> 01:16:09,631
Maybe it would have been better if it hadn't rained so much?

1119
01:16:09,720 --> 01:16:10,709
No.

1120
01:16:11,800 --> 01:16:13,677
It was perfect.

1121
01:16:14,880 --> 01:16:15,869
Phew.

1122
01:16:18,880 --> 01:16:21,189
This is just the beginning.

1123
01:16:21,680 --> 01:16:24,592
There will be many days ahead.

1124
01:16:25,480 --> 01:16:26,469
Isn't it fun?!

1125
01:16:33,000 --> 01:16:33,989
Position

1126
01:16:35,640 --> 01:16:37,358
Posyne

1127
01:16:37,960 --> 01:16:40,155
The prettiest girl in the world

1128
01:16:43,560 --> 01:16:47,553
You want to go to Dad, right? I know.

1129
01:16:50,840 --> 01:16:51,829
Okay.

1130
01:16:54,920 --> 01:16:58,515
No one can prepare you for having a child.

1131
01:16:58,680 --> 01:17:02,992
When I hold the baby in my arms, I feel like it's my responsibility now.

1132
01:17:03,920 --> 01:17:07,754
Nobody can prepare you for love and fear.

1133
01:17:09,360 --> 01:17:11,316
You're so lovely.

1134
01:17:12,360 --> 01:17:14,351
You were such an ugly baby.

1135
01:17:14,720 --> 01:17:16,392
More chimpanzee than baby, really.

1136
01:17:17,040 --> 01:17:18,553
I remember when I first saw you.

1137
01:17:18,640 --> 01:17:21,552
I was glad we didn't live near the London Zoo.

1138
01:17:22,760 --> 01:17:25,832
Let's see, give me the baby. Let's see if he squirms.

1139
01:17:25,920 --> 01:17:27,717
- Still... - Of course he squirming.

1140
01:17:27,880 --> 01:17:30,269
- Look - He can do anything.

1141
01:17:30,400 --> 01:17:32,356
- Look - Bye.

1142
01:17:34,560 --> 01:17:36,039
Baby.

1143
01:17:37,080 --> 01:17:40,675
No one can prepare me for the love of people who love me

1144
01:17:42,920 --> 01:17:44,319
For the indifference of friends without children

1145
01:17:44,400 --> 01:17:46,356
There's nothing I can prepare for either

1146
01:17:46,440 --> 01:17:50,228
Should we go to Uncle Jay's place? No, never mind, I'm fine.

1147
01:17:50,600 --> 01:17:52,795
The moment when you have to move to a house you can barely afford

1148
01:17:52,880 --> 01:17:55,713
comes so fast, it's surprising.

1149
01:17:56,280 --> 01:17:59,272
Look at what I found. Look who it is!

1150
01:17:59,880 --> 01:18:02,189
Team! Sorry.

1151
01:18:04,920 --> 01:18:08,595
Suddenly, time travel felt unnecessary.

1152
01:18:08,720 --> 01:18:10,756
Because every single moment of life was so much fun.

1153
01:18:10,920 --> 01:18:13,388
"Happy birthday, Poppy."

1154
01:18:18,280 --> 01:18:19,713
What's your name?

1155
01:18:19,840 --> 01:18:22,229
I think Horace would be good. Sure, sounds nice.

1156
01:18:22,320 --> 01:18:24,515
I heard that as a godfather, the most important thing

1157
01:18:24,600 --> 01:18:26,955
is never to bring a gift smaller than the child.

1158
01:18:27,120 --> 01:18:29,429
Shut up, you big shot.

1159
01:18:29,560 --> 01:18:33,519
Don't worry, I didn't bring any gifts either. I don't know anyway; I have no brain.

1160
01:18:33,640 --> 01:18:37,792
I didn't expect you to come. This isn't like Harry's kids' parties.

1161
01:18:37,960 --> 01:18:41,111
Right. Mary, I was ripped off. They said there would be free drinks, so I came.

1162
01:18:43,000 --> 01:18:45,116
As you know, I hate kids.

1163
01:18:45,320 --> 01:18:46,912
But where's KitKat?

1164
01:18:47,280 --> 01:18:50,272
I don't know. She said she'd be here around three.

1165
01:18:50,360 --> 01:18:53,670
And I even made special purple cupcakes.

1166
01:18:54,160 --> 01:18:57,072
- You're here! - The tiger comes when I speak, they say.

1167
01:18:58,800 --> 01:19:01,314
Let's wait until Aunt KitKat gets here.

1168
01:19:02,320 --> 01:19:03,833
- Hello. - Jimmy.

1169
01:19:04,000 --> 01:19:05,479
Where's my sister?

1170
01:19:06,840 --> 01:19:08,990
- I thought she already came. - No, she hasn't.

1171
01:19:10,880 --> 01:19:12,393
This sucks.

1172
01:19:12,920 --> 01:19:14,592
What are you talking about?

1173
01:19:16,000 --> 01:19:20,596
We had a little fight this morning. We drank because of something small...

1174
01:19:21,520 --> 01:19:25,035
I drove over because she said she was coming here.

1175
01:19:25,160 --> 01:19:27,549
I told her we should meet here...

1176
01:19:27,920 --> 01:19:31,356
There's this song by Baz Luhrmann called "Sunscreen."

1177
01:19:31,520 --> 01:19:33,670
He said worrying about the future

1178
01:19:33,760 --> 01:19:38,038
is as pointless as chewing bubblegum to solve an equation.

1179
01:19:38,680 --> 01:19:40,750
The really serious problems in a person's life

1180
01:19:40,920 --> 01:19:44,674
are always things they haven't even thought about yet.

1181
01:19:58,240 --> 01:19:59,389
What happened?

1182
01:20:01,200 --> 01:20:02,872
We fought.

1183
01:20:03,400 --> 01:20:04,389
And

1184
01:20:05,720 --> 01:20:08,234
I think I was a little drunk.

1185
01:20:10,040 --> 01:20:11,917
- How are you? - Not good.

1186
01:20:12,240 --> 01:20:16,756
When did you leave? Where were you? Tell me the exact time and address.

1187
01:20:26,560 --> 01:20:29,120
We're here, sorry, sorry.

1188
01:20:29,400 --> 01:20:30,628
Come in.

1189
01:20:31,680 --> 01:20:33,238
Oh my god.

1190
01:20:33,560 --> 01:20:35,596
- Hi - I brought him.

1191
01:20:35,920 --> 01:20:37,911
Does a little baby live here?

1192
01:20:38,080 --> 01:20:42,232
Yes, he's very excited. He's downstairs.

1193
01:20:42,840 --> 01:20:44,910
Happy birthday, Poppy.

1194
01:20:47,120 --> 01:20:49,680
Sorry for bringing KitKat.

1195
01:20:49,800 --> 01:20:53,509
- I thought you'd drive yourself - It turned out that way.

1196
01:20:54,760 --> 01:20:56,876
- Are you okay? - I'll tell you later.

1197
01:20:59,240 --> 01:21:01,196
I'm worried about KitKat.

1198
01:21:03,200 --> 01:21:05,191
Yeah, I know.

1199
01:21:05,880 --> 01:21:08,872
While we were having tea, he just kept drinking wine.

1200
01:21:09,480 --> 01:21:11,914
Jimmy was being awful,

1201
01:21:12,040 --> 01:21:15,112
and he wouldn't even touch the purple cupcake.

1202
01:21:15,920 --> 01:21:18,229
I have to fix something.

1203
01:21:20,400 --> 01:21:21,389
Right.

1204
01:21:22,400 --> 01:21:24,072
But

1205
01:21:24,800 --> 01:21:29,032
if anything is going to get fixed, he has to want it to.

1206
01:21:30,480 --> 01:21:31,469
Maybe.

1207
01:21:32,520 --> 01:21:33,999
Or maybe not.

1208
01:21:37,960 --> 01:21:40,235
What happened?

1209
01:21:40,560 --> 01:21:45,315
You're the coolest person in the world. Just as amazing as my wife.

1210
01:21:47,040 --> 01:21:48,996
Maybe

1211
01:21:50,120 --> 01:21:51,872
I'm the problem child.

1212
01:21:52,760 --> 01:21:56,469
Every family has one of those people, right?

1213
01:21:56,840 --> 01:21:59,798
Someone who isn't good at school and messes everything up.

1214
01:21:59,920 --> 01:22:01,911
Someone whose life gets tangled up.

1215
01:22:02,440 --> 01:22:04,556
Maybe I'm the troublemaker in my family.

1216
01:22:05,680 --> 01:22:06,669
No.

1217
01:22:07,720 --> 01:22:08,869
Not at all.

1218
01:22:15,960 --> 01:22:18,952
Okay, I'll tell you a secret.

1219
01:22:19,120 --> 01:22:21,350
You have to promise to keep it quiet.

1220
01:22:21,640 --> 01:22:24,518
- We always kept each other's secrets, didn't we? - Did we?

1221
01:22:24,960 --> 01:22:27,599
Never, never, never, ever.

1222
01:22:27,760 --> 01:22:30,035
Never, never, never, never, never.

1223
01:22:30,640 --> 01:22:33,313
Promise you won't say a word?

1224
01:22:33,600 --> 01:22:34,589
Yeah.

1225
01:22:40,320 --> 01:22:42,754
I can travel through time.

1226
01:22:45,840 --> 01:22:48,115
Why do I have to stand in the cupboard under the stairs?

1227
01:22:48,240 --> 01:22:51,676
Because I need to go back in time and act differently.

1228
01:22:51,800 --> 01:22:53,677
Oppa, this is so fun when you do this.

1229
01:22:53,800 --> 01:22:56,030
Hold my hand, close your eyes tight.

1230
01:23:13,080 --> 01:23:16,470
Oh my god! Oh my god!

1231
01:23:17,200 --> 01:23:21,034
This is unbelievable!

1232
01:23:25,960 --> 01:23:26,995
Are you kidding me?

1233
01:23:27,080 --> 01:23:30,789
We could go back anytime, but you brought me to the worst party of my life?

1234
01:23:30,920 --> 01:23:32,990
Unfortunately, let's go.

1235
01:23:35,920 --> 01:23:38,150
- I have something to do - What is it?

1236
01:23:38,320 --> 01:23:41,312
I'm not meeting Jimmy Kinkade.

1237
01:23:41,440 --> 01:23:42,839
Hurry, come inside.

1238
01:23:44,760 --> 01:23:48,116
- But I was about to fall in love with him! - Not this time.

1239
01:23:57,880 --> 01:24:01,190
Who's the prettiest? Jennifer?

1240
01:24:01,320 --> 01:24:03,834
- Yeah - She's amazing!

1241
01:24:03,960 --> 01:24:06,758
- I like your skirt, Jennifer. - Thanks.

1242
01:24:06,880 --> 01:24:09,314
Okay, I get it.

1243
01:24:09,480 --> 01:24:13,553
So someone else slept with him, not me.

1244
01:24:13,960 --> 01:24:15,871
It's all in the past.

1245
01:24:18,880 --> 01:24:20,552
Wait a second, Jimmy.

1246
01:24:21,640 --> 01:24:23,551
- Sorry. - You know me?

1247
01:24:23,680 --> 01:24:25,511
Of course.

1248
01:24:26,120 --> 01:24:28,759
I know you really well, sorry.

1249
01:24:28,880 --> 01:24:31,269
We should have done this from the start.

1250
01:24:37,320 --> 01:24:40,471
Happy New Year, everyone. Happy New Year.

1251
01:24:40,600 --> 01:24:42,511
Go back to the pantry quickly.

1252
01:24:45,040 --> 01:24:46,189
Awesome!

1253
01:24:46,480 --> 01:24:49,199
- What happens now? - Only God knows.

1254
01:24:49,320 --> 01:24:50,912
What I want is starting right now,

1255
01:24:51,000 --> 01:24:53,992
that you don't hang out with those dirty bad guys, because they are dirty and bad.

1256
01:24:54,400 --> 01:24:56,755
When did it get this serious?

1257
01:24:56,880 --> 01:24:59,189
Ever since I felt like I might lose you.

1258
01:25:01,960 --> 01:25:04,679
Brace yourself; things might be weird.

1259
01:25:05,240 --> 01:25:07,196
Things might have changed.

1260
01:25:13,560 --> 01:25:14,913
Oh my god.

1261
01:25:15,040 --> 01:25:17,235
- Why? - Jay.

1262
01:25:17,360 --> 01:25:19,157
- That Jay? - Yeah.

1263
01:25:19,840 --> 01:25:23,196
He's so cute, seriously.

1264
01:25:24,800 --> 01:25:25,789
Right.

1265
01:25:26,400 --> 01:25:27,913
Let's go outside.

1266
01:25:33,880 --> 01:25:35,393
Welcome.

1267
01:25:36,040 --> 01:25:39,077
Mom is planning something new.

1268
01:25:44,400 --> 01:25:46,994
I have an idea.

1269
01:25:47,120 --> 01:25:49,839
- I understand what you mean. - Have a cookie and then help me.

1270
01:25:51,440 --> 01:25:53,749
Leave the rest for Uncle D.

1271
01:25:56,240 --> 01:25:58,515
We're just tidying up.

1272
01:25:58,920 --> 01:26:00,911
- Are you okay? I missed you. - Yeah.

1273
01:26:01,440 --> 01:26:04,079
- Your mom wants help gardening. - Sure.

1274
01:26:06,280 --> 01:26:11,070
Just tidy up, we just need to pull out the dead stuff because it's a mess.

1275
01:26:11,240 --> 01:26:14,073
It turned out how we wanted, didn't it?

1276
01:26:14,240 --> 01:26:15,593
- The dead ones. - Look at this.

1277
01:26:18,280 --> 01:26:20,714
All messed up because of bugs.

1278
01:26:33,640 --> 01:26:37,315
- How did it turn out? - Completely satisfying.

1279
01:26:37,720 --> 01:26:41,235
That's great! Tell me more.

1280
01:26:41,320 --> 01:26:43,311
Can you prepare dinner?

1281
01:26:43,400 --> 01:26:45,277
If I don't finish by six, I'll probably get fired.

1282
01:26:45,440 --> 01:26:48,750
Yeah, this is totally what I want to do.

1283
01:26:48,880 --> 01:26:51,952
Let's see, who is the coolest person in the world?

1284
01:26:52,120 --> 01:26:56,955
If you come to Dad, I'll feed you yummy snacks.

1285
01:27:04,080 --> 01:27:05,559
Bye, baby.

1286
01:27:09,480 --> 01:27:10,913
You wait here for a sec.

1287
01:27:11,040 --> 01:27:13,474
Stay here, I'll be right back.

1288
01:27:25,840 --> 01:27:27,751
Dad, can I talk to you for a minute?

1289
01:27:27,840 --> 01:27:29,671
Sure.

1290
01:27:31,680 --> 01:27:35,389
- Can't we go back before childbirth? - No, you didn't say that.

1291
01:27:35,520 --> 01:27:40,674
Before you were born is fine, but the exact sperm and the exact moment

1292
01:27:40,840 --> 01:27:42,068
created this child.

1293
01:27:42,160 --> 01:27:45,789
If anything is even slightly different, a different child will be born.

1294
01:27:47,920 --> 01:27:52,596
So everything until yesterday was the same? Will we lose everything?

1295
01:27:53,520 --> 01:27:55,795
Just like other people.

1296
01:27:55,960 --> 01:27:57,837
I see, that's interesting.

1297
01:27:58,640 --> 01:28:01,313
This is a headache. I love you, Dad. I gotta go.

1298
01:28:25,720 --> 01:28:27,631
- Go home. - No.

1299
01:28:27,720 --> 01:28:29,312
I'll stay here until I find a way

1300
01:28:29,400 --> 01:28:33,188
so this never happens again.

1301
01:28:46,040 --> 01:28:47,712
Can you leave now?

1302
01:29:01,040 --> 01:29:03,429
You have to break up with Jimmy, right?

1303
01:29:04,440 --> 01:29:05,919
Forever.

1304
01:29:06,880 --> 01:29:08,074
And

1305
01:29:08,240 --> 01:29:10,276
I have to quit drinking,

1306
01:29:13,200 --> 01:29:15,077
stop working,

1307
01:29:17,120 --> 01:29:21,193
and date someone else,

1308
01:29:21,920 --> 01:29:24,593
someone nice and boring.

1309
01:29:27,600 --> 01:29:28,794
Right.

1310
01:29:32,120 --> 01:29:35,237
Being nice doesn't always mean being boring.

1311
01:29:35,360 --> 01:29:36,634
Who said that?

1312
01:29:37,760 --> 01:29:39,239
Matt Damon?

1313
01:29:39,640 --> 01:29:40,959
Sounds good.

1314
01:29:41,960 --> 01:29:43,552


1315
01:29:43,640 --> 01:29:46,871


1316
01:29:46,960 --> 01:29:51,476


1317
01:29:51,600 --> 01:29:52,589


1318
01:29:53,440 --> 01:29:56,398


1319
01:29:56,760 --> 01:29:58,751


1320
01:30:00,440 --> 01:30:01,589


1321
01:30:01,720 --> 01:30:04,109


1322
01:30:04,240 --> 01:30:07,994


1323
01:30:08,120 --> 01:30:10,350


1324
01:30:17,040 --> 01:30:19,952


1325
01:30:20,080 --> 01:30:23,436


1326
01:30:23,600 --> 01:30:26,717


1327
01:30:27,000 --> 01:30:28,513
Where's Forge?

1328
01:30:29,200 --> 01:30:31,668
Over there! Hi!

1329
01:30:31,800 --> 01:30:34,519
Hi! Bye.

1330
01:30:34,640 --> 01:30:36,835
How have our baby been?

1331
01:30:40,440 --> 01:30:42,351
Let's have another one.

1332
01:30:44,160 --> 01:30:47,197
No way, I don't want to.

1333
01:30:49,080 --> 01:30:52,072
I'm hurting, and I'll get really, really fat.

1334
01:30:52,200 --> 01:30:54,475
Well, I did get a little chubby.

1335
01:30:54,840 --> 01:30:56,796
Ask Mom to give us a younger sister.

1336
01:30:56,920 --> 01:31:00,993
No, tell Dad he likes having only one child.

1337
01:31:02,760 --> 01:31:07,675
Luckily, we're young and careless, so soon enough you'll have your own family.

1338
01:31:07,800 --> 01:31:11,156
Truly amazing, Forge Lake, Third Generation Bangryeong.

1339
01:31:11,280 --> 01:31:14,272
She's about to break the women's 10-meter Olympic record.

1340
01:31:14,400 --> 01:31:18,518
You did it! You succeeded! That's great.

1341
01:31:18,640 --> 01:31:21,359
Truly amazing, you did a wonderful job.

1342
01:31:21,480 --> 01:31:22,879
You sleep well even with all this noise.

1343
01:31:23,000 --> 01:31:25,275
Can you help me out? I'm dying of nerves.

1344
01:31:25,360 --> 01:31:27,669
What should I wear for dinner with our bestselling author?

1345
01:31:27,800 --> 01:31:30,360
I'll feed our little troublemakers and be right back.

1346
01:31:30,480 --> 01:31:31,674
Okay, thanks.

1347
01:31:32,040 --> 01:31:33,439
Try again.

1348
01:31:33,880 --> 01:31:36,474
How about this one?

1349
01:31:36,600 --> 01:31:39,114
Cool, good choice, nice.

1350
01:31:39,240 --> 01:31:42,391
No, look closely at this, this is...

1351
01:31:43,040 --> 01:31:46,032
I don't know, I hate it, I don't like it.

1352
01:31:46,360 --> 01:31:48,078
- Right - It's too boring,

1353
01:31:48,600 --> 01:31:51,478
And I look a bit overweight.

1354
01:31:51,600 --> 01:31:54,398
Yeah, it looks a bit boring and fat. I hate it too.

1355
01:31:56,280 --> 01:31:58,111
How about this one?

1356
01:31:58,520 --> 01:32:00,476
Awesome, that's it.

1357
01:32:00,960 --> 01:32:03,235
No, the cleavage is too deep.

1358
01:32:03,360 --> 01:32:04,349
Really?

1359
01:32:04,440 --> 01:32:06,476
- Good - This doesn't have too much cleavage.

1360
01:32:06,600 --> 01:32:09,672
No, I can't wear these shoes; I look like a prostitute.

1361
01:32:09,800 --> 01:32:13,156
- Then take off the heels - Then I'll look completely stubby.

1362
01:32:13,280 --> 01:32:15,794
Do you prefer looking like a prostitute or a dwarf?

1363
01:32:16,920 --> 01:32:19,036
Warning, I'm warning you.

1364
01:32:22,720 --> 01:32:23,755
Great!

1365
01:32:23,880 --> 01:32:24,869
No.

1366
01:32:28,800 --> 01:32:29,789
No!

1367
01:32:30,840 --> 01:32:32,910
I like that one.

1368
01:32:33,200 --> 01:32:38,320
This is underwear to wear under the dress, dummy.

1369
01:32:40,720 --> 01:32:42,995
- This one? - Not bad.

1370
01:32:43,640 --> 01:32:46,473
- Or this one? - Are you testing me? They're the same thing.

1371
01:32:46,600 --> 01:32:47,589
No!

1372
01:32:48,160 --> 01:32:49,195
No?

1373
01:32:49,600 --> 01:32:51,750
Okay, this one seems alright.

1374
01:32:52,200 --> 01:32:53,838
Yeah, it looks cool.

1375
01:32:54,320 --> 01:32:55,958
- Really? - Yeah.

1376
01:32:56,080 --> 01:32:58,435
Yeah, okay, it's fine.

1377
01:33:00,080 --> 01:33:01,798
Or how about blue?

1378
01:33:01,920 --> 01:33:03,558
- Blue? - Sure.

1379
01:33:03,720 --> 01:33:06,871
The one you wore first? The one you said looked boring and fat?

1380
01:33:06,960 --> 01:33:09,110
So, it wasn't actually boring or fat?

1381
01:33:09,200 --> 01:33:13,159
- Yeah, which one do you think is better? - I don't know, I feel like I'm going crazy.

1382
01:33:13,280 --> 01:33:16,192
- I think blue is better. - Yeah.

1383
01:33:17,680 --> 01:33:20,274
Alright, let's go with this one then.

1384
01:33:20,400 --> 01:33:22,231
It's really cool.

1385
01:33:22,360 --> 01:33:23,509
- Really? - Yep.

1386
01:33:23,640 --> 01:33:25,232
Okay, thank you.

1387
01:33:25,760 --> 01:33:27,432
Oh my god.

1388
01:33:27,880 --> 01:33:29,632
Where's Forge?

1389
01:33:29,920 --> 01:33:31,751
I left it downstairs.

1390
01:33:32,240 --> 01:33:35,550
You didn't leave the door to the room with the manuscript open, did you?

1391
01:33:36,600 --> 01:33:38,272
I don't think so.

1392
01:33:39,120 --> 01:33:41,509
Look at me, look me in the eyes and tell me.

1393
01:33:41,640 --> 01:33:45,076
Tell me what to do, my life is over.

1394
01:33:45,200 --> 01:33:47,794
Just a second, I'll step out. Two minutes, no, one minute.

1395
01:33:47,920 --> 01:33:49,592
Where are you going!

1396
01:33:50,680 --> 01:33:53,831
Don't answer the phone! What am I supposed to do?

1397
01:33:54,040 --> 01:33:55,758
I think I should answer the phone.

1398
01:33:55,840 --> 01:33:58,877
If you answer the phone, I'll kill you along with the phone.

