- Did I ask you to play Nick Cave music? - Yes, I did.

1549
01:45:49,440 --> 01:45:50,873
Thanks.

1550
01:45:51,280 --> 01:45:53,589
Want to listen to this?

1551
01:45:57,920 --> 01:46:00,434
Read it out loud, I have time.

1552
01:46:01,120 --> 01:46:05,750
The Romans must have annoyed each other with their noses.

1553
01:46:05,960 --> 01:46:09,430
Maybe that's why the Romans became such an impatient people.

1554
01:46:09,560 --> 01:46:12,791
Anyway, when I look at Mr. Wells' Roman nose, I always get irritated...

1555
01:47:48,680 --> 01:47:50,989
How are the kids?

1556
01:47:51,120 --> 01:47:52,633
What about the kids?

1557
01:47:53,680 --> 01:47:55,875
There aren't many, right?

1558
01:47:56,960 --> 01:47:57,949
What?

1559
01:47:58,680 --> 01:48:00,671
There are only two.

1560
01:48:03,480 --> 01:48:05,869
That's more than the Chinese government allows anyway.

1561
01:48:07,800 --> 01:48:10,473
Still, in my opinion...

1562
01:48:11,560 --> 01:48:14,358
- I think we need another baby for insurance. - What?

1563
01:48:14,480 --> 01:48:15,913
If one of them is really smart,

1564
01:48:16,000 --> 01:48:18,230
the other will spend their whole life thinking they're stupid.

1565
01:48:18,320 --> 01:48:22,711
So if we have a third, we'll just have two happy idiots.

1566
01:48:25,480 --> 01:48:27,152
What do you think?

1567
01:48:31,520 --> 01:48:33,988
It was the hardest decision of my life.

1568
01:48:34,520 --> 01:48:39,435
Because if I say yes to the future, it means saying goodbye forever to Dad.

1569
01:48:41,240 --> 01:48:43,231
How about waiting a bit?

1570
01:48:46,120 --> 01:48:47,269
Sure.

1571
01:48:48,120 --> 01:48:50,111
You're right.

1572
01:48:54,720 --> 01:48:56,392
Have you thought about it?

1573
01:48:59,440 --> 01:49:00,793
Now?

1574
01:49:03,120 --> 01:49:04,269
Now?

1575
01:49:11,720 --> 01:49:12,709
Okay.

1576
01:49:14,080 --> 01:49:15,069
Fine.

1577
01:49:16,600 --> 01:49:17,635
Really?

1578
01:49:19,920 --> 01:49:22,593
Dad always wanted us to have more siblings.

1579
01:49:23,400 --> 01:49:24,389
So...

1580
01:49:26,800 --> 01:49:29,473
Anyway, even if I try, it might not happen.

1581
01:49:30,080 --> 01:49:31,069
Right.

1582
01:49:39,840 --> 01:49:41,831
It could be tonight.

1583
01:49:42,480 --> 01:49:46,393
You have no idea how well I know the way to the hospital.

1584
01:49:51,160 --> 01:49:52,991
Want to be alone for a bit?

1585
01:49:53,920 --> 01:49:55,831
I'll go down to the ground floor.

1586
01:50:12,280 --> 01:50:15,272
...It's 17 to 20. A really close match.

1587
01:50:15,360 --> 01:50:19,035
This is a match between two physically perfect athletes in history.

1588
01:50:19,200 --> 01:50:22,033
The crowd, captivated by the young athlete,

1589
01:50:22,120 --> 01:50:24,873
gets lost in the glamorous memories of the veteran.

1590
01:50:26,880 --> 01:50:28,871
Wow, I won.

1591
01:50:29,720 --> 01:50:32,029
I won for the first time in years.

1592
01:50:32,560 --> 01:50:34,516
You've finally improved your skills.

1593
01:50:35,200 --> 01:50:38,829
What's my prize? Excluding the Olympic gold medal, of course.

1594
01:50:39,880 --> 01:50:42,474
- You'll have to settle for a kiss - A kiss?

1595
01:50:42,880 --> 01:50:44,233
A kiss?

1596
01:50:49,560 --> 01:50:51,516
Got it.

1597
01:50:52,880 --> 01:50:54,393
Today is the day.

1598
01:50:56,360 --> 01:50:57,713
That's right.

1599
01:50:58,520 --> 01:51:00,715
It's the last moment of time gained through luck.

1600
01:51:02,040 --> 01:51:04,554
I think the baby is about to come.

1601
01:51:24,760 --> 01:51:26,079
Congratulations.

1602
01:51:33,120 --> 01:51:34,599
My son.

1603
01:51:37,960 --> 01:51:39,552
My dad.

1604
01:51:44,520 --> 01:51:48,798
Is there anything I can do? What would you like to do?

1605
01:51:50,560 --> 01:51:53,233
Well...

1606
01:51:55,040 --> 01:51:56,712
There is one thing.

1607
01:51:57,040 --> 01:51:59,110
I'd like to take a short walk.

1608
01:51:59,240 --> 01:52:03,119
It's completely against the rules, but if we don't change anything,

1609
01:52:03,480 --> 01:52:06,790
as long as just us are careful, nothing will happen.

1610
01:52:07,320 --> 01:52:08,912
I want to take a walk.

1611
01:52:39,320 --> 01:52:42,312
Keep going, keep going.

1612
01:52:44,160 --> 01:52:45,479
You need to throw it lower.

1613
01:52:50,200 --> 01:52:51,189
You totally lost.

1614
01:53:00,960 --> 01:53:02,279
I'm tired.

1615
01:53:03,280 --> 01:53:04,679
Thank you, Dad.

1616
01:53:20,200 --> 01:53:23,033
It's time for me to end my story.

1617
01:53:23,560 --> 01:53:27,030
Like every family, we adapted to life without a father.

1618
01:53:27,160 --> 01:53:29,037
And everything was fine.

1619
01:53:29,840 --> 01:53:33,992
With the changing seasons, we started riding the rhythm of the traditions we kept,

1620
01:53:34,480 --> 01:53:36,869
and time went by just like before.

1621
01:53:38,240 --> 01:53:40,879
We also got used to Kitcat looking happy again.

1622
01:53:41,840 --> 01:53:44,354
And for Kitcat, who became a mother,

1623
01:53:44,720 --> 01:53:47,393
though she wasn't always a strong or safe mom,

1624
01:53:48,840 --> 01:53:50,193
finally,

1625
01:53:50,320 --> 01:53:53,995
I learned the last lesson of time travel.

1626
01:53:54,800 --> 01:53:58,110
I went one step further than my father did.

1627
01:54:08,800 --> 01:54:11,109
I'll watch the kids.

1628
01:54:12,320 --> 01:54:14,880
No, I'll watch them.

1629
01:54:15,000 --> 01:54:17,434
Alright, go watch the kids, lazy old man.

1630
01:54:17,840 --> 01:54:21,833
Now I don't time travel anymore, not even for one day.

1631
01:54:22,280 --> 01:54:27,593
I just try to live each day fully and happily,

1632
01:54:28,000 --> 01:54:31,629
thinking of it as my special yet ordinary last day, just like I traveled back for this day.

1633
01:54:31,920 --> 01:54:34,639
Goodbye, you're already downstairs, good job, thank you so much.

1634
01:55:02,920 --> 01:55:06,629
Come on, sit down.

1635
01:55:06,760 --> 01:55:08,159
Pogi? Pogi!

1636
01:55:09,760 --> 01:55:12,558
It's okay.

1637
01:55:20,960 --> 01:55:21,949
We travel through time with every single day of our lives.

1638
01:55:43,440 --> 01:55:46,273
The best we can do is

1639
01:55:46,560 --> 01:55:48,710
enjoy this wonderful journey.

1640
01:55:48,920 --> 01:55:51,388
Yeah, yeah...

1641
01:55:51,880 --> 01:55:54,599
Okay, see you then.

1642
01:56:37,560 --> 01:56:39,471
Bye.

1643
01:56:51,800 --> 01:56:53,870
See ya later.

